{"anchor": {"begin": [138, 0, 169.33], "end": [138, 0, 255.33], "env": "lemma", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 63, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "A.6", "source_sha256": "f2a5588933ffaacec5a6f4ce4d53eda3544b1c4dbb8de9c3ff9940c08bf0b824", "statement": "Lemma A.6. The function H is positive and smooth up to Z = 0 from the right. Every fixed derivative is bounded on bounded nonnegative intervals. The field K(r, t) = c ∞ s −A H(2 τ /s), s = r 2 /2, (A.33) is independent of z, satisfies ∂ t K = ( ∂ rr + r −1 ∂ r − r −2 )K, and has K r < 0. Its profile is E pow (X)H(2d/X), smooth with all η -derivatives extending continuously to η = ±1 from the interior.", "title": null}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code)", "confidence": "high", "coverage": "full", "note": "Split into the heat equation ∂t K = (∂rr + r^−1 ∂r − r^−2)K for K = C s^(−A) H(2τ/s), positivity and smoothness of H on [0, ∞) with derivative bounds (uniform on the whole half-line), K_r < 0 for τ > 0, and joint smoothness of the heat-switched profile on X > 0, η ∈ [−1, 1]. K is z-independent by construction.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.FlatCutoff.edge": "d4934426f8f410446a5bb761", "NavierStokes.HeatTailEdit.edit": "0ef0c257ed81c191a2dbafbe", "NavierStokes.HeatTailEdit.multiplier": "818ee6ebfd6090f4aa027ce7", "NavierStokes.HeatTailEdit.outgoingEdit": "94c5236bb61aad58b09c5ea1", "NavierStokes.HeatTailEdit.outgoingProfile": "0d9d7ff4f20585063c00dbf8", "NavierStokes.HeatTailEdit.switch": "867535869bb6c3b913d7a1b1", "NavierStokes.HeatTailEdit.switchStart": "d353c907700ae6af6b2670b1", "NavierStokes.OutgoingSchedule.Parameters": "a80493cad406265f1e6eb0a1", "NavierStokes.OutgoingSchedule.Parameters.P": "f39f6dcb64b4182f0d43a39a", "NavierStokes.OutgoingSchedule.Parameters.dropLength": "804ec912a150442ec24ec5b9", "NavierStokes.OutgoingSchedule.Parameters.endpoint": "7781ca39